From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-controller: 989 - reconcile-sweep stale bss and sta rows

The bss sweep (mapc_sync_bss_sweep) deletes bss NOT IN r->iflist, but
r->iflist was never reconciled at iface granularity: a ghost iface from a
re-flash was merely set enabled=false and kept, so it stayed in the sweep's
own protect-set forever. Add cntlr_node_sweep_ifaces(), a per-iface mirror of
cntlr_node_sweep_radios keyed on bss->tsp (set fresh for every iface present
in the AP Operational BSS TLV), run right after the radio sweep. r->iflist is
then the current picture and the existing bss sweep removes the ghost rows.

sta had no sweep at all -- a backhaul bSTA left by a re-flash never emits a
disassoc event, so mapc_del_sta was never called and the row was immortal.
Add mapc_sync_sta_sweep(): DELETE ... WHERE agent_almac=? AND macaddr NOT IN
(live stalist), called after the Topology Response stalist persistence. Both
sweeps no-op on an empty/oversized report so a half-parsed CMDU cannot wipe
the tables.

Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/cntlr.c
+++ b/src/cntlr.c
@@ -1195,6 +1195,28 @@
 	}
 }
 
+/* Drop ifaces of confirmed radios whose BSS was not in the latest AP
+ * Operational BSS TLV (bss->tsp older than this pass), so r->iflist -- and
+ * thus mapc_sync_bss_sweep's NOT IN protect-set -- is the current picture,
+ * not the union of every BSSID a radio ever had. Runs after
+ * cntlr_node_sweep_radios so only surviving (confirmed) radios are walked. */
+void cntlr_node_sweep_ifaces(struct controller *c, struct node *n, time_t since)
+{
+	struct netif_radio *r = NULL;
+	struct netif_iface *ni = NULL, *tmp;
+
+	list_for_each_entry(r, &n->radiolist, list) {
+		list_for_each_entry_safe(ni, tmp, &r->iflist, list) {
+			if (ni->bss->tsp >= since)
+				continue;	/* confirmed this pass */
+			mactable_del_entry(c->mac_table, ni->bss->bssid, MAC_ENTRY_FBSS);
+			free(ni->bss);
+			list_del(&ni->list);
+			free(ni);
+		}
+	}
+}
+
